\f0\fs24 \cf2 Four doors... but only two are real! The others? Fake. A small architectural trick designed to create perfect visual harmony and frame the grand fireplace as if it were a throne. But the twist doesn\'92t end there: above each door, Latin mottos appear, little pearls of wisdom celebrating the pleasures of the table, eating well to live better, as we might say today. And then there are the original designs, preserved as treasures in the museum\'92s archive, revealing a meticulous plan: plant motifs, animals, mythological figures... nothing is left to chance. Every detail of these doors is a clue to the refined, almost obsessive vision with which the Bagatti Valsecchi brothers built their world.\
